1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MADS PEDERSEN GRAM
2 CONT
2 CONT Begravet i Karlsøy 26.12.1787:  https://www.digitalarkivet.no/view/267/pg00000002164520
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Skifte 1789''' (s.495a): [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081205670895]
2 CONT
2 CONT Great-great-great-great-great-grandson of Ludvig Munk.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT The Hanson Jorgenson Robertson Genealogy, A history of three Lines of Ancestors and their Descendants, by Hans G. Jorgenson. P. 36:
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was born in 1717 and died 1787.  He was married to Margrete Gronbeck, born 1725 and died 1763, daughter of Hans Gronbeck from Bergen (1693 - 1762). Mads and Margrete Pedersen Gram were the parents of Jorgen Madsen Gram."
2 CONT
2 CONT I would like to add a note that Mads was the third son of Peder Hansen Gram who was a State Church Minister (prest) in southern Norway and committed a misdeameanor (which we know from elsewhere that he took up with a young girl of
2 CONC  perhaps 16 without an official announcement of courting, which was frowned upon. 
2 CONT Peder Hansen Gram  was dismissed and sent north to Karlsoy. 
2 CONT So Peder Hansen Gram was the first Gram in Karlsoy, and is the forerunner of the entire Gram dynasty which later became Baptist and emigrated to America. 
2 CONT We are looking at whether Mads Pedersen Gram stayed in the south or went to Karlsoy, but he married Margrete Gronbeck  from Bergen.  (note added by David Clounch, Nov 21, 2017)
2 CONT --------------------
