1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Synneve's mtDNA (the DNA the mother passes on to her children) was U5a1b1e. Description of this DNA haplogroup: Specific mitochondrial haplogroups are typically found in different regions of the world, and this is 
2 CONC due to unique population histories. In the process of spreading around the world, many populations—with their special mitochondrial haplogroups—became isolated, and specific haplogroups concentrated in geographic regions. Today, w
2 CONC e have identified certain haplogroups that originated in Africa, Europe, Asia, the islands of the Pacific, the Americas, and even particular ethnic groups. Of course, haplogroups that are specific to one region are sometimes found
2 CONC  in another, but this is due to recent migration.
2 CONT
2 CONT The mitochondrial super-haplogroup U encompasses haplogroups U1-U7 and haplogroup K. Haplogroup U5, with its own multiple lineages nested within, is the oldest European-specific haplogroup, and its origin dates to approximately 50
2 CONC ,000 years ago. Most likely arising in the Near East, and spreading into Europe in a very early expansion, the presence of haplogroup U5 in Europe pre-dates the expansion of agriculture in Europe. Haplogroup U5a1—a lineage within 
2 CONC haplogroup U5—arose in Europe approximately 30,000 years ago, and is mainly found in northwest Europe. In the context of its rather ancient origin, the modern distribution of haplogroup U5a1 suggests that individuals bearing this 
2 CONC haplogroup were part the initial expansion tracking the retreat of ice sheets from Europe. (from www.familytreedna.com)
